OK. So script.json can be text-led with `on_screen_text`, or `{"chunks": []}`. This video has no on-screen text (no captions/overlays) and no dialogue. The law says: a genuinely no-dialogue, no-caption piece may use `{"chunks":[]}` plus `{"captions":{"required":false}}` in promise.json.

Let me now set up files. Write:
- jobs/<id>/script.json: {"chunks": [], "on_screen_text": []} — hmm, better keep minimal: {"chunks": []}
- jobs/<id>/promise.json: {"captions":{"required":false}, ...}

Let me check promise.json schema quickly.
